mon with other  tim burton projects like 1990s edward  scissorhands than most other superhero  movies it's certainly too macabre for  small children which is why there was  such a huge backlash after warner  brothers deployed misleadingly  kid-friendly marketing including  mcdonald's happy meal toys  but as long as you keep the kitties away  from this flick you'll have a great time  you will however notice a major  departure and tone once you move on  burton and keaton both left the caped  crusader behind following batman returns  and the decision makers at warner  brothers rattled by the backlash decided  gotham city needed to get a lot less  gothic  a more accurate title for 1995's batman  forever might be the bright knight  returns fans have been describing joel  schumacher's pair of batman movies as  torturous viewing experiences for years  they're certainly a lot more colorful  and less serious than either burton  movie and as a certain cultural critic  once asked why so serious  1995's batman forever was a commercially  successful film though reviews were  mediocre at best it is also utterly  consumed by the all-encompassing black  hole of kinetic absurdity that is  mid-90s jim carrey fresh off megastar  turns in 1994's ace ventura pet  detective and the mask carries  relentless rubber-faced riddler devours  this movie much to the chagrin of  co-star tommy lee jones carrie told noor  macdonald that jones was very upfront  about his disdain for him and he went  like to hug me and said i  hate you  and jones wasn't the only cast member  having a rough time effectively  immobilized by his heavy bat suit vel  kilmer left the batman franchise after  batman forever in order to work on  movies where he got to act instead of  just fill a rubber costume still batman  forever is entertaining and an important  step in the dark knight cinematic  evolution notably it marks the first  time bruce wayne's introduction to dick  grayson is captured on the silver screen  while t