k is doing his best to play a  batman who has lived long enough to  become the villain  if your purpose in this endeavor is to  watch every batman movie then the 2017  edit of justice league overseen by  director joss whedon and 2021's zack  snyder's justice league the re-edit  released on hbo max both do the trick  these two films tell essentially the  same story and are equally relevant to  batman's overall place in the pop  cultural universe but if time isn't a  factor since the snyder cut is literally  twice as long as whedon's two hour  justice league we think even the most  adamant snyder critics would probably  admit his take is better whedon's film  has its moments but it ultimately  amounts to a bland exercise in pushing a  handful of intellectual properties  through the market demanded motions  meanwhile the snyder cut is a maximalist  cataclysm of r-rated action fantasy  lunacy 2017's justice league is a  corporate product it is not art the  snyder cut is also a corporate product  but maybe it is art either way one thing  is absolutely certain there's definitely  more batman stuff in the snyder cut just  as there is more of literally everything  else  the batman open to generally positive  feedback and appears as though it will  more than likely produce a sequel or two  however for right this second it's a  provisionally standalone film whose  identity within batman's film ubra has  yet to fully take shape but even though  it's the most recent movie and thus  logically the last one you should watch  there are actually a few different  options for placement of the batman in  your movie marathon from the standpoint  of its central character's evolution the  batman could fit before the burton  schumacher series though it's not an  origin story in the traditional sense  robert pattinson's depiction of bruce  wayne is a hero who's a little  underbaked he only starts growing into a  hyper-competent crime smasher resembling  the guy from 1989's batman at the  movie's conclusion then again since  culture and world events of the 2000s  heavily inform nolan's trilogy maybe it  makes more sense to watch the movies in  their real world release order as the  batman director matt reeves infuses  sentiments of the 2010s and early 2020s  into his gotham city saga we do not  recommend watching the batman  immediately before or after the 1966  batman because the tonal clash between  paul dano and frank gorshin's  interpretations of the riddler may cause  the viewer some internal whiplash or  psychic damage gorsuchian's riddler  never successfully kills anybody while  danos riddler kills a whole score of  folks in nasty ways  no word though on how tommy lee jones  feels about either of their performances  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  batman are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]

